### 4. System Architecture

#### 4.1 Core Layers

🔹 1. Data Ingestion Layer  
Sources include:
- Public datasets (Kaggle vehicle specs, GitHub)
- NHTSA APIs (recalls, complaints, investigations)
- Parts catalogs (public metadata)
- User submissions and community uploads
- Forum and video metadata (ethical scraping only)

🔹 2. AI Extraction Layer  
AI pipelines handle:
- NLP parsing of forum threads
- Video transcription + step-by-step extraction (Whisper + LLMs)
- Entity recognition for parts, torque specs, tools, sequences, and failure modes

Example Transformation:  
Input: “Tighten the head bolts to 85 ft-lbs in a criss-cross sequence.”  
Output:
json {   "component": "cylinder_head",   "torque_spec": "85 ft-lbs",   "sequence": "criss-cross",   "unit": "ft-lbs",   "confidence": 0.92 } 

🔹 3. Knowledge Graph Layer  
Graph structure enables rich relationships:
- Vehicle → has → Engine → contains → Component → has → Torque_Spec / Procedure / Failure_Mode

🔹 4. Verification & Trust Layer  
- Community voting and reputation system
- Multi-source cross-validation
- Confidence scoring per fact
- Git-style forking and merging of procedures

🔹 5. API & Interface Layer  
- Natural language search (“2003 F250 head bolt torque”)
- VIN-based lookup
- Mobile-first mechanic UI
- Open developer API with full documentation

---

### 5. Data Model

#### 5.1 Core Entities
- Vehicle (year, make, model, trim, VIN pattern)
- Engine / Drivetrain
- Component
- Procedure (steps, tools, warnings)
- Specification (torque, clearance, fluid specs)
- Issue / Failure_Mode
- Part (OEM/cross-reference)

#### 5.2 Key Relationships
- Vehicle → HAS_ENGINE → Engine
- Engine → CONTAINS → Component
- Component → HAS_SPEC → Specification
- Component → HAS_PROCEDURE → Procedure
- Component → FAILS_WITH → Issue → RESOLVED_BY → Procedure

---

### 6. AI Pipeline

Inputs: Forums, YouTube videos, public PDFs, user uploads.  
Processing:
1. Transcription & chunking
2. Entity extraction & normalization
3. Relationship inference
4. Confidence scoring with source citation

Outputs: Structured, versioned, queryable knowledge with provenance.

Multimodal extensions (vision models for diagrams) are planned.

---

### 7. Legal & Compliance Framework

Do NOT:
- Store or redistribute full OEM manuals
- Scrape against terms of service aggressively

Do:
- Extract non-copyrightable facts (torque values, procedures derived from community)
- Prioritize NHTSA public data and user-generated content
- Provide source references and confidence scores

Safe data types: factual specs, aggregated insights, community guides.

